    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Math Talk: The Hour Hand",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Your teacher will give you a time. Identify the radian angle measure that the hour hand rotates through if it starts at 3 p.m.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Create a visual display for the following functions. Include a graph of the function from at least \\(\\text-4\\pi\\) to \\(4\\pi\\) radians, the maximum and minimum value of the function, and the period of the function. Label any intersections…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The \\(y\\)-axis is a line of symmetry for one of the two graphs. Which one? Explain how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Recall that a symmetry is a rigid transformation that takes a figure onto itself (not counting a transformation that leaves every point where it is). For example, the graph of \\(y=(x-3)^2\\) has reflection symmetry across the line \\(x=3\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find a reflection symmetry of the graph of \\(y=\\sin(\\theta)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find a rotation symmetry of the graph of \\(y=\\sin(\\theta)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: The Big Picture for Cosine and Sine",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find a translation symmetry of the graph of \\(y=\\sin(\\theta)\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use graphing technology to graph the functions \\(y = \\cos(\\theta)\\) and \\(y = \\sin(\\theta)\\) on the same axes.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Identify two points where the graphs intersect—one with a negative \\(\\theta\\)-coordinate, and one with a positive \\(\\theta\\)-coordinate. What is the exact \\(\\theta\\)-coordinate for each point? Explain or show how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What are the \\(y\\)-coordinates of the points of intersection? Explain or show how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What could be the value of \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\) if \\(\\sin(\\theta)=0\\)? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The functions \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\) and \\(\\sin(\\theta)\\) are both periodic, meaning their values repeat at regular intervals. Since the period of cosine and sine is \\(2\\pi\\), the values of these functions repeat any time the input is changed by…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Notice that between \\(\\text-2\\pi\\) and \\(0\\), and then between 0 and \\(2\\pi\\), the same wave pattern repeats. Both positive and negative values for \\(\\theta\\) can be thought of through the lens of the unit circle with positive values…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The \\(\\theta\\)-intercepts of the graph are at all integer multiples of \\(\\pi\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The relative maximums are at \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) and any integer multiple of \\(2\\pi\\) from there.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The relative minimums are at \\(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\) and any integer multiple of \\(2\\pi\\) from there.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The graph of \\(y= \\cos(\\theta)\\) is also periodic, repeating every time the input changes by a multiple of \\(2\\pi\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The \\(\\theta\\)-intercepts are at \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) and any integer multiple of \\(\\pi\\) from there.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L11-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Cosine and Sine Together",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The relative maximums are at 0 and any integer multiple of \\(2\\pi\\) from there.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
